    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d169">

                <pb facs="0383" n="337" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v02/pg337"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72/4673½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-05-10">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">10 May, 1917</hi>
                        </date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I think our list is now
                    complete, namely:<list>
                        <item>Mr. Elihu Root,</item>
                        <item>Mr. Charles R. Crane,</item>
                        <item>Dr. John R. Mott,</item>
                        <item>Mr. Cyrus H. McCormick,</item>
                        <item>Mr. S. R. Bertron,</item>
                        <item>Mr. James Duncan, as the representative of labor,</item>
                        <item>Mr. Charles Edward Russell.<anchor n="20a" xml:id="d169-f1"/>
                        </item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <p>I have only just learned of the willingness of Mr. Russell to serve and am
                    sending him a note today to learn the earliest hour at which he would be ready
                    to leave. I think it would be wise now to give out the names of the
                    Commissioners and supply the Press with as full information as they desire about
                    the several members. I am enclosing the account of Mr. Russell from <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Who’s Who</hi>.<anchor n="20b" xml:id="d169-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>Faithfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Woodrow Wilson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d169-f1" n="20a" xml:id="d169-f1-content">
                <p>For the final composition of the Commission, see <ref
                        target="frus1918Russiav01#pg_109">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1918, Russia, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>, p. 109</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d169-f2" n="20b" xml:id="d169-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
